Wow, a much larger response than I expected in a very short amount of
time! Since there seems to indeed be interest, I'll go into more detail
about my work on this 'project'.

The vast majority of the sounds I used are from game making software,
specifically RPG Making software, specifically RPG Maker and RPG Maker
XP. This works well because all of the sounds are roughly the same
quality and type, and the game has a very uniform feeling, like an old
NES or SNES RPG type feel. This approach is something I enjoy, and I
couldn't imagine playing the game any other way.

As far as infringing upon copyrights, I hadn't given it a whole lot of
thought to tell you the truth and a handful of sounds are actually from
licenced, non-'maker' software, such as snippets from Age of Wonders or
a stray sound from an SNES RPG or whatnot. I realize this might be a
problem somehow, and I could easily remove those if need be, but I
haven't given copyrights much thought really. Example: When the word
'secret door' appears with my soundset, the 'Legend of Zelda'
traditional secret door noise plays. I can't describe the sound in
words but for those who know of it it's a funny little treat that is
enjoyable to myself. In any case, I must stress that those little
'throwbacks' are pretty few in number, but I felt I should mention that
they exist.

All in all, I approached this for pure entertainment really, and until
now hadn't thought much about the finer details.


